tools.description:
Get full metadata for a specific RedBison tool by its id (slug).

Returns: Full JSON metadata for the tool: { id, name, description, url, category, subcategory?, keywords[] }.
Example input: {"id":"jwt-decoder"}

List all tool categories and subcategories available on RedBison.

Returns: JSON array of { category, count } entries covering the full RedBison catalog.
Example input: {}

Return server status, name, version, and uptime info. Use this to monitor the MCP server.

Returns: JSON { status, name, version, startedAt, timestamp }.
Example input: {}

Base64-encode a UTF-8 string.

Returns: Base64-encoded string (UTF-8 safe).
Example input: {"text":"hello world"}

Base64-decode a string back to UTF-8.

Returns: UTF-8 decoded plain text.
Example input: {"text":"aGVsbG8gd29ybGQ="}

Percent-encode a string for use in URLs.

Returns: Percent-encoded string suitable for URL query values.
Example input: {"text":"hello world & friends"}

Percent-decode a URL-encoded string.

Returns: Percent-decoded plain text.
Example input: {"text":"hello%20world%20%26%20friends"}

Pretty-print an HTML fragment.

Returns: Pretty-printed HTML string with normalized indentation.
Example input: {"html":"<div><p>hi</p><p>there</p></div>","indent":2}

Pretty-print an XML document.

Returns: Pretty-printed XML string with normalized indentation.
Example input: {"xml":"<root><a>1</a><b>2</b></root>","indent":2}

Format a SQL query with keyword uppercasing and line breaks before major clauses.

Returns: Formatted SQL query with keywords on new lines.
Example input: {"sql":"select id,name from users where active=true order by name"}

Convert text to a URL-safe slug.

Returns: URL-safe slug (lowercase, dashes).
Example input: {"text":"Hello, World! 2026"}

Remove duplicate lines from text while preserving first-occurrence order.

Returns: Text with duplicate lines removed (order preserved).
Example input: {"text":"apple\nbanana\napple\ncherry","caseInsensitive":false,"trim":true}

Collapse runs of whitespace inside each line to a single space and trim ends.

Returns: Text with runs of whitespace collapsed to a single space.
Example input: {"text":"hello    world   foo"}

Join lines with a separator (comma by default). Empty lines are skipped.

Returns: Single-line string with items joined by the chosen separator.
Example input: {"text":"apple\nbanana\ncherry","separator":", ","quote":false}

Split a delimited string into one item per line.

Returns: Multi-line string, one item per line.
Example input: {"text":"apple, banana, cherry","separator":",","trim":true}

Generate random human names.

Returns: JSON array of random human name strings.
Example input: {"count":3}

Generate random-looking (non-deliverable) test email addresses.

Returns: JSON array of random email address strings.
Example input: {"count":3,"domain":"example.com"}

Generate cryptographically random numbers in a range.

Returns: JSON array of generated numbers.
Example input: {"min":1,"max":100,"count":5,"mode":"integer"}

Generate placeholder lorem ipsum text.

Returns: Lorem ipsum text of the requested size.
Example input: {"unit":"paragraphs","count":2}

Compute the equated monthly installment (EMI) for a loan.

Returns: JSON { emi, totalInterest, totalPayment } for the loan.
Example input: {"principal":500000,"annualRatePercent":8.5,"months":240}

Compute simple interest: I = P × r × t.

Returns: JSON { interest, total } computed as P·r·t.
Example input: {"principal":10000,"annualRatePercent":5,"years":3}

Compute compound interest: A = P(1 + r/n)^(nt).

Returns: JSON { interest, total } computed as P(1+r/n)^(nt).
Example input: {"principal":10000,"annualRatePercent":5,"years":10,"compoundsPerYear":12}

Calculate Body Mass Index in metric (kg/cm) or imperial (lb/in) units.

Returns: JSON { bmi, category } (Underweight / Normal / Overweight / Obese).
Example input: {"weight":70,"height":175,"units":"metric"}
